```

Note: This implementation only covers a small subset of Markdown syntax and maps them to their corresponding HTML tags. It assumes that the input string contains at most one space after the header hash symbol (`#`) and that emphasis and bold formatting can be intermixed. This implementation also assumes that only either the first occurrence or both occurrences of an emphasized or bolded text should be converted to HTML (hence the need to extract substrings). A more robust implementation would handle these edge cases and cover a wider range of Markdown formatting constructs.

